@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "koroneiki"

Feature: Koroneiki Team and Contact Role API Permissioning
	Testing Koroneiki Team API Permissioning functionality in relation to Contact Roles.

Teardown:
	* I tear down the permissions for a koroneiki contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" set for a non permissioned user
	* I tear down the permissions for a koroneiki contact role with the name "Default Team Role" set for a non permissioned user
	* I tear down the permissions for a koroneiki account with the name "Koroneiki Automotive" set for a non permissioned user
	* I tear down the contacts on koroneiki with the following email addresses
	| koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the contact roles on koroneiki with the following names
	| Default Team Role |
	* I tear down the teams on koroneiki with the following names
	| Development Team |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| Koroneiki Automotive |

Scenario: Assign contact role to contact attempt
	Koroneiki contacts should not be able to be assigned to team contact roles on teams by non permissioned users.

	Given I create a contact on koroneiki with the following values
	| Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Koroneiki                                |
	| Language      | English                                  |
	| Last Name     | Contact1                                 |
	| Middle Name   | User                                     |
	And I create a contact role on koroneiki with the following values
	| Description | This is the default role for teams |
	| Name        | Default Team Role                  |
	| Type        | Team                               |
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code         | KORAUTO                              |
	| Description  | Test automotive account on koroneiki |
	| Fax Number   | 555-555-1234                         |
	| Name         | Koroneiki Automotive                 |
	| Phone Number | 555-555-5678                         |
	| Region       | United States                        |
	| Status       | Approved                             |
	| Tier         | Regular                              |
	| Website      | www.koroneikiautomotive.com          |
	And I create a team with the name "Development Team" for the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	And I assign contacts with the following email addresses to the team "Development Team"
	| koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	And I attempt to assign the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the team "Development Team" to the following roles as a non permissioned user	
	| Default Team Role |
	Then the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" assigned the team "Development Team" should not have the contact role "Default Team Role"
	And the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" assigned the team "Development Team" should have the contact role "Member"
	And the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" assigned the team "Development Team" should not have the contact role "Member" visible to a non permissioned user

Scenario: View contact role from contact attempt
	Koroneiki team contact roles assigned to contacts should not be viewable by non permissioned users.

	Given I create a contact on koroneiki with the following values
	| Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Koroneiki                                |
	| Language      | English                                  |
	| Last Name     | Contact1                                 |
	| Middle Name   | User                                     |
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code         | KORAUTO                              |
	| Description  | Test automotive account on koroneiki |
	| Fax Number   | 555-555-1234                         |
	| Name         | Koroneiki Automotive                 |
	| Phone Number | 555-555-5678                         |
	| Region       | United States                        |
	| Status       | Approved                             |
	| Tier         | Regular                              |
	| Website      | www.koroneikiautomotive.com          |
	And I create a team with the name "Development Team" for the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	And I create a contact role on koroneiki with the following values
	| Description | This is the default role for teams |
	| Name        | Default Team Role                  |
	| Type        | Team                               |
	And I assign contacts with the following email addresses to the team "Development Team"
	| koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	And I assign the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the team "Development Team" to the following roles	
	| Default Team Role |
	Then the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" assigned the team "Development Team" should have the contact role "Default Team Role"
	And the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" assigned the team "Development Team" should have the contact role "Member"
	And the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" assigned the team "Development Team" should not have the contact role "Default Team Role" visible to a non permissioned user
	And the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" assigned the team "Development Team" should not have the contact role "Member" visible to a non permissioned user

