Scenario: Assign contact role to contact as permissioned user
	Koroneiki contacts should be able to be assigned to team contact roles on teams by permissioned users.

	Given I create a contact on koroneiki with the following values
	| Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Koroneiki                                |
	| Language      | English                                  |
	| Last Name     | Contact1                                 |
	| Middle Name   | User                                     |
	And I create a contact role on koroneiki with the following values
	| Description | This is the default role for teams |
	| Name        | Default Team Role                  |
	| Type        | Team                               |
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code         | KORAUTO                              |
	| Description  | Test automotive account on koroneiki |
	| Fax Number   | 555-555-1234                         |
	| Name         | Koroneiki Automotive                 |
	| Phone Number | 555-555-5678                         |
	| Region       | United States                        |
	| Status       | Approved                             |
	| Tier         | Regular                              |
	| Website      | www.koroneikiautomotive.com          |
	And I create a team with the name "Development Team" for the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	And I assign contacts with the following email addresses to the team "Development Team"
	| koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	And I set the permissions for a team with the name "Development Team" to have the following values for a non permissioned user
	| Assign Contact | true |
	And I set the permissions for a contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to have the following values for a non permissioned user
	| View | true |
	And I set the permissions for the contact role "Default Team Role" to have the following values for a non permissioned user
	| Assign Contact | true |
	And I assign the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the team "Development Team" to the following roles as a permissioned user	
	| Default Team Role |
	Then the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" assigned the team "Development Team" should have the contact role "Default Team Role"
	And the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" assigned the team "Development Team" should have the contact role "Member"

Scenario: Remove contact role to contact as permissioned user
	Koroneiki contacts should be able to be removed from team contact roles on teams by permissioned users.

	Given I create a contact on koroneiki with the following values
	| Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Koroneiki                                |
	| Language      | English                                  |
	| Last Name     | Contact1                                 |
	| Middle Name   | User                                     |
	And I create a contact role on koroneiki with the following values
	| Description | This is the default role for teams |
	| Name        | Default Team Role                  |
	| Type        | Team                               |
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code         | KORAUTO                              |
	| Description  | Test automotive account on koroneiki |
	| Fax Number   | 555-555-1234                         |
	| Name         | Koroneiki Automotive                 |
	| Phone Number | 555-555-5678                         |
	| Region       | United States                        |
	| Status       | Approved                             |
	| Tier         | Regular                              |
	| Website      | www.koroneikiautomotive.com          |
	And I create a team with the name "Development Team" for the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	And I assign contacts with the following email addresses to the team "Development Team"
	| koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	And I set the permissions for a team with the name "Development Team" to have the following values for a non permissioned user
	| Assign Contact | true |
	And I set the permissions for a contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to have the following values for a non permissioned user
	| View | true |
	And I set the permissions for the contact role "Default Team Role" to have the following values for a non permissioned user
	| Assign Contact | true |
	And I assign the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the team "Development Team" to the following roles as a permissioned user	
	| Default Team Role |
	And I remove the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the team "Development Team" from the following roles as a permissioned user	
	| Default Team Role |
	Then the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" assigned the team "Development Team" should not have the contact role "Default Team Role"
	And the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" assigned the team "Development Team" should have the contact role "Member"

Scenario: Assign contact role to contact attempt by newly non permissioned user
